How can I implement the Quick Sort algorithm in MATLAB to sort an array of integers in descending order?
Here is the sample code for implementing the Quick Sort algorithm in MATLAB:
function sortedArray = quickSort(arr)
    if length(arr) <= 1
        sortedArray = arr;
        return;
    end
    pivotIndex = ceil(length(arr)/2);
    pivot = arr(pivotIndex);
    arr(pivotIndex) = [];
    leftArray = arr(arr < pivot);
    rightArray = arr(arr >= pivot);
    sortedArray = [quickSort(leftArray), pivot, quickSort(rightArray)];
end
To sort the array in descending order, we need to modify the code to sort the right array first, then the pivot, and then the left array. Here's the modified code:
function sortedArray = quickSortDesc(arr)
    if length(arr) <= 1
        sortedArray = arr;
        return;
    end
    pivotIndex = ceil(length(arr)/2);
    pivot = arr(pivotIndex);
    arr(pivotIndex) = [];
    leftArray = arr(arr >= pivot);
    rightArray = arr(arr < pivot);
    sortedArray = [quickSortDesc(leftArray), pivot, quickSortDesc(rightArray)];
end
To use this function, simply call it with your array as the input argument. For example, to sort the array [3, 5, 1, 7, 2] in descending order, you would call:
sortedArray = quickSortDesc([3, 5, 1, 7, 2]);
The resulting sorted array would be [7, 5, 3, 2, 1].

