What are some effective methods for preventing the spread of viruses in JavaScript? 
Here are three examples of code you can implement:
1. Implement a function that adds an event listener to all buttons and links on your webpage that prevents default behavior when clicked:
```javascript
function preventDefaultBehavior() {
  const buttons = document.getElementsByTagName('button');
  const links = document.getElementsByTagName('a');

  for(let i = 0; i < buttons.length; i++) {
    buttons[i].addEventListener('click', function(event) {
      event.preventDefault();
    });
  }

  for(let i = 0; i < links.length; i++) {
    links[i].addEventListener('click', function(event) {
      event.preventDefault();
    });
  }
}
```
2. Use regular expressions to sanitize user input and prevent injection attacks:
```javascript
function sanitizeInput(input) {
  const regex = /[&<>"'`=\/]/g;
  const sanitizedInput = input.replace(regex, '');

  return sanitizedInput;
}
```
3. Implement a function that validates user input to ensure that it meets certain criteria before allowing it to be processed:
```javascript
function validateInput(input) {
  const regex = /^[a-zA-Z0-9!@#$%^&*()_+\-=\[\]{};':"\\|,.<>\/?]*$/;

  if(regex.test(input)) {
    return true;
  } else {
    return false;
  }
}
